# Wireless survey and software-defined radio: RECEIVE ONLY. The image is for
# incident response and threat hunting, so the radio slice answers one question
# ("is something transmitting here that is not in the asset inventory?") and
# never transmits itself. rtl-sdr (rtl_test, rtl_power sweeps to CSV) and gqrx
# work with receive-only RTL2832U dongles; gqrx pulls the gr-osmosdr *library*
# it needs on its own. Dropped on purpose (snapshot-menu 0.2.4): gnuradio and
# gr-osmosdr (flowgraph tooling nobody builds during an incident, ~350 MiB with
# SciPy/PyQt), soapysdr-tools (only useful with per-device modules and GNU Radio)
# and hackrf (transmit-capable hardware; red-team gear, not IR). aircrack-ng is
# here for airodump-ng's passive 802.11 survey. (kismet is not in trixie:
# upstream apt repo only, not pinned here.)
aircrack-ng
rtl-sdr
gqrx-sdr
